nds  exactly i mean i mean if you're in a job  that you hate  which hopefully darwin is not because  darwin works for me  but if you're in a job that you really  don't like um and you just want to get  out as fast as possible  then it might make sense to put a  portion of that money maybe 10 000  pounds or something  into rent to rent to get some instant  cash flow and you focus  more on instant cash flow if you like  your job  and you're happy you're thinking about  just building wealth and growing your  portfolio  then it might make sense to put the  fifty thousand pounds into into  the portfolio but i feel like there's a  conflict of interest of me giving advice  right here right now  because darwin is a member of my staff  who's actually behind the camera  um who always you know what he always  does this because he'll we'll be driving  he's my videographer and he'll say to me  send me out do you know when you do a  property video and i'll go  and then ask me a question i'll say  that's a really good question you know  what and you'll go yeah and i'll say  this sunday at 7 pm he's like yeah i'm  like i'm doing a q a  right crack your joke thing but anyway  if you've got questions  whether you work for me whether you're  one of my students whether you're brand  new today  comment below did that happen that  helped their darwin good  all right brandon carr i'm wanting to  get into property and property investing  and i'm starting a job as an estate  agent is this a good idea to get me into  property so i can learn all the ropes  i think it is a good idea yes um  if you're young and you know you you you  feel like doing good job as an estate  agent i did this i worked for bestow  eaves countrywide i did it for about  three or six months  i did learn quite a lot as an estate  agent i learned how to speak to estate  agents  i didn't learn about property investing  in a state agency they'll teach you how  to be a good estate agent  they'll teach you how to sell houses 